      "stem": "A 55-year-old man reports progressive breathlessness on exertion. BP is 164/52 mm Hg and his radial pulse rises and collapses rapidly. The apex is displaced. A high-pitched early diastolic murmur is most audible along the left sternal edge when he leans forward. Which lesion best explains these findings?",
